<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- A-39b: Liquibase-owned copy of the Spring Batch 6 postgres DDL,
         table-prefixed per service (PRG_BATCH_) for single-writer cleanliness
         (R-34), EXIT_MESSAGE widened to TEXT so CRDB-driver cause chains are never
         truncated.

         LIQUIBASE-SQL-EXCEPTION: this is autogenerated FRAMEWORK DDL owned by Spring
         Batch, not schema this project designs. Hand-transcribing 6 tables and 3
         sequences into typed tags would fork the framework's own schema and make the
         next Batch upgrade a manual diff, which is the vendor-lock the pure-XML rule
         exists to prevent, not an instance of it. Same precedent as PRR 002, PRW 002
         and PIX 002.

         Every CREATE carries IF NOT EXISTS, and that is NOT the retrofit the v1
         baseline forbids: one file creates nine objects and CockroachDB DDL is not
         transactional, so a pod SIGKILLed mid-migration leaves it half-applied with
         no changelog row. That is also why this changeset carries no precondition
         (A-81: a precondition sampling one of the nine reads a half-applied file as
         complete and skips the rest forever).

         validCheckSum ANY is kept for the same forward-looking reason PIX kept it
         (A-82) even though prg-004 has never run anywhere: a future edit to the
         vendored framework DDL must not fail validation on a database that already
         carries PRG history. It is APPLICABILITY that must stay preserved for this
         file, not the byte-for-byte checksum. -->
    <changeSet id="prg-004-batch-metadata" author="dcre">
        <validCheckSum>ANY</validCheckSum>
        <sqlFile path="db/changelog/2026/08/batch-metadata-prg.sql" splitStatements="true"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
